  "notes": [
    "Admission requires exact hands/replay evidence, finite gradients, positive MGDA worst-group alignment at every optimizer step, >=1pct probe movement every seed, preservation weight/disagreement gates, positive pooled and median seed delta, >=2/3 positive seeds, all holdout opponents positive, and both seats positive. Failure closes this gate/expert-pair route; no dose or checkpoint rescue.",
    "All gzip counts and SHA256 values matched; all 12 NPZ shards were finite with exact expert probability mass. Replay reconstructed all three endpoints exactly and emitted all 96 optimizer metrics; applied worst alignment was positive at every step. Full AlphaHoldem suite: 308 passed."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "Matched MGDA gate training completed exactly 12,288 training and 18,432 paired evaluation hands. MGDA achieved positive worst-group alignment on all 96 exactly replayed steps and all three gates moved materially, but pooled holdout delta was -10.50 bb/100 CI [-34.47,+13.47], seed deltas +0.03/-6.39/-25.14, two holdout opponents were negative (-37.75 and -31.02), and seat1 was -28.47.",
    "conclusion": "Conflict-averse optimization solved the measured training-gradient conflict but worsened untouched holdout generalization relative to the ordinary high-dose gate. This is explicit proxy reversal, not a failure inferred from too few hands or failure to beat Slumbot. The Standard10/diverse_league5 decision-gate route is closed without further dose, checkpoint, or scale rescue.",
    "decision": "CLOSE_DECISION_GATE_EXPERT_PAIR_PROXY_REVERSAL",
    "next_step": "Return to the broader research portfolio. Do not scale PSRO selectors, whole-hand routers, or this decision-gate pair. Prioritize a learned policy-improvement target whose small-scale proxy has demonstrated external directional alignment with the Standard10 greedy contract; retain Standard10 as the only reproducible frontier parent and require early exact-contract 20k evidence before million-hand expansion."
  },
